        "predicate": "article",
        "object": "## What are the current Kalshi odds?\n\nOdds as of October 3, 2026 at 20:15 UTC. Each price is the middle of the bid and the ask, read as a probability; the market lists 37 outcomes and 30 thousand contracts traded in the last 24 hours.\n\n- **Above 4.1050**: 1% (bid 0 cents, ask 2 cents; 8 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.1000**: 34% (bid 0 cents, ask 68 cents; 6 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.1150**: 33% (bid 0 cents, ask 66 cents; 4 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.0800**: 25% (bid 0 cents, ask 49 cents; 4 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.0900**: 34% (bid 0 cents, ask 68 cents; 2 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.0950**: 19% (bid 0 cents, ask 37 cents; 1 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.0850**: 35% (bid 0 cents, ask 70 cents; 1 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n- **Above 4.1200**: 9% (bid 0 cents, ask 18 cents; 1 thousand contracts in 24 hours)\n\nPrices change with every trade; the [live Kalshi market](https://kalshi.com/markets/kxaaagasdoh/ohio-gas-price/kxaaagasdoh-26oct04) is the current figure.\n\n## What is our view?\n\nWe have no model of our own for this market, so the odds above are the traders' consensus and not an independent estimate. For calibration: in our sample of settled Economics markets, the Kalshi mid-price a day before close scored a Brier error of 0.1108 (a coin-flip price scores 0.25; lower is better).\n\n## How does this market resolve?\n\n> If average regular gas prices for Ohio are strictly greater than $3.9400 on Oct 4, 2026 according to AAA, then the market resolves to Yes.\n\nClose: October 4, 2026 at 03:59 UTC. Expected settlement: October 4, 2026 at 14:00 UTC. Settlement source: [AAA](https://gasprices.aaa.com/?state=OH). Full terms: [Kalshi contract terms](https://assets.kalshi.com/contract_terms/AAAGAS.pdf).\n\n## What could move the odds?\n\n- The release of the named data series (the settlement source), or a revision to it.\n- For daily published series such as gas prices, the latest published value relative to the strike: these series move a fraction of a cent a day, so the odds only swing when the value sits near a strike.\n- A rules clarification or settlement-source change published by Kalshi on the market page.\n- Order-book depth: thin books move on small orders, so a large price move on little volume says little.\n\n## How reliable are markets like this one?\n\nAcross 116 settled Economics markets in our sample (Kalshi, 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-03), the Kalshi mid-price about 24 hours before close had a Brier error of 0.1108; a coin-flip price scores 0.25 and lower is better. Contracts quoted at 5 cents or less settled YES 0% of the time (20 markets); contracts quoted at 95 cents or more settled YES 97% (31 markets). The sample covers a few weeks, so it is a guide to how markets like this have behaved, not a guarantee of how this one will settle.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What are the odds on \"Ohio gas prices tomorrow\"?\n\nAs of October 3, 2026 at 20:15 UTC, Kalshi implies Above 3.9550 at 50%, Above 3.9600 at 50%, and Above 3.9700 at 50%. These move with every trade; the live market is at https://kalshi.com/markets/kxaaagasdoh/ohio-gas-price/kxaaagasdoh-26oct04.\n\n### What does a price on Kalshi mean as a probability?\n\nA contract that pays $1 if the outcome happens and trades at 45 cents implies about a 45% chance, before fees and ignoring the small gap between the bid and the ask. We take the middle of the bid and the ask.\n\n### When does this market close and settle?\n\nIt closes October 4, 2026 at 03:59 UTC and is expected to settle October 4, 2026 at 14:00 UTC, in about 8 hours from the time of writing.\n\n### Where does the settlement data come from?\n\nKalshi names AAA (https://gasprices.aaa.com/?state=OH) as the settlement source. The full contract terms are at https://assets.kalshi.com/contract_terms/AAAGAS.pdf.\n\n### Can I bet on this on Kalshi?\n\nKalshi is a federally regulated exchange (a CFTC-designated contract market). Whether you can trade depends on your location and eligibility under Kalshi's terms. The market is at https://kalshi.com/markets/kxaaagasdoh/ohio-gas-price/kxaaagasdoh-26oct04.\n\n### Is this financial advice?\n\nNo. This wire reports a market's odds and its publisher's analysis from public information. Prediction-market contracts can lose their entire price.\n\n## About these odds\n\nOdds are a snapshot taken October 3, 2026 at 20:15 UTC from Kalshi's public market data and are not a prediction. This uses public information only and is not financial advice; prediction-market contracts can lose their entire price. The 561 Group, which publishes this wire and Koios.News, may trade on Kalshi, including in this market."
